{"week":17,"opponent":"DET","home":false,"pf":23.0,"pa":20.0,"off_snaps":85,"epa_per_play":0.06814,"pass_rate":0.6588,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6136,"def_epa_per_play":-0.1449}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2020,"team":"CAR","distance":0.3959,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Joe Brady"},{"season":2019,"team":"MIA","distance":0.4744,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.505,"shared":15,"play_caller":null},{"season":2018,"team":"MIN","distance":0.511,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2019,"team":"CLE","distance":0.5123,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2025,"team":"LA","distance":0.6034,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Chris Shula"},{"season":2021,"team":"TEN","distance":0.6768,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"TEN","distance":0.764,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2019,"team":"LA","distance":0.7724,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"TEN","distance":0.7791,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Packers went 13-3 in 2019 and outscored opponents 376 to 313. The offense ranked 9th in EPA per play and the defense 15th in EPA allowed, so neither side stood out much. What set them apart was the 2nd highest neutral-script pass rate and the highest dime usage in the league.","offense":"The Packers offense was well above average by EPA per play. They threw more than almost anyone relative to the situation, even when the score did not call for it. Their biggest outliers in how they lined up were the 3rd lowest pistol usage in the league. Aaron Rodgers ran the passing game, with Davante Adams leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Packers defense was about average by EPA allowed per play. It was much better against the pass than the run, ranking 7th and 30th. Kenny Clark was as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise was Za'Darius Smith, who had 13.5 sacks, after not being a regular on this defense last season. In terms of scheme, they had the highest dime usage in the league.","special":"The Packers were about average in how often they went for it on fourth down. Their kickers made 92% of field goals, which was one of the best in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the offensive line, about 25% of the money on the books. The offense also brought back more of its roster than most, with 97% of its snaps going to players who were on the team the year before.","players":"Aaron Rodgers played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 4,002 yards. Davante Adams was the clear top target with 23% of the looks and 997 receiving yards. Aaron Jones handled most of the work in the backfield with 66% of the carries. On defense, Za'Darius Smith led the team with 13.5 sacks and Kevin King picked off 5 passes.","coaching":"Matt LaFleur called the offense, and the defensive play caller for this season is not in the coaching data. Their offense looked most like the 2020 Panthers under Joe Brady and the 2019 Dolphins. Their defense looked most like the 2025 Rams under Chris Shula and the 2021 Titans.","trends":"The offense went from 11th in EPA per play in 2018 to 9th in 2019, about where it was. The defense moved from 27th in EPA allowed per play in 2018 to 15th in 2019, a big step forward. The biggest change in approach was pistol usage, which went from 3% to 0%.","notes":"FTN did not start charting plays until 2022, so play action, motion, RPO and screen rates are not available for 2019. Everything else, including personnel, formations and coverage, is complete for this season."}}